OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1791811202
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G2/2
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Mon 26 Oct to Mon 9 Nov
OL,6,FHigh pressure brings settled weather
OL,7,Fat first, but there are signs for a
OL,8,Fgradual shift away from high pressure
OL,9,Fand towards a more changeable pattern,
OL,10,Fwith areas of low pressure moving
OL,11,Ftowards the northwestern UK from the
OL,12,FNorth Atlantic. Showers or longer
OL,13,Fspells of rain are likely, with the
OL,14,Fwettest and windiest weather typically
OL,15,Fin the west and northwest, and drier
OL,16,Fconditions favoured in southern and
OL,17,Feastern parts. A trend to more widely
OL,18,Funsettled conditions is possible into
OL,19,FNovember. Whilst some occasional
OL,20,Fcolder interludes will be possible at
OL,21,Ftimes, temperatures are likely to be
OL,22,Fnear or a little above normal for the
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fperiod as a whole.
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
